{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290647-the-order-of-reason-for-the-man","id":1290647,"title":"The order of reason - for the man?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-21T21:21:37-08:00","id":1290647,"title":"The order of reason - for the man?","content":"Ok, I'm rusty. Last time I read mage, it was a year ago. And it was progenitor, M20, toybox, and a few others. <br /> <br /> Question. Can I say that the order of reason, who transformed into the technocracy later on, was a champion of the common man? That they were the first ones to try and give magic into the common man. To try and give magic and power to the masses in the form of 'technology'. And so that's why people rallied to them, and their dedication and unity and cooperation, caused the people to rally to them. And that's how they won the war. By putting magic and power into the hands of the common man. <br /> <br /> Is what I said, correct, or at least, a reasonable interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T22:18:18-08:00","id":1290653,"title":"","content":"I think it's somewhat misleading - but it's certainly what the Order believes.<br /> <br /> We know that mages were engaged with Sleeper communities for millennia before the Order's founding - the ancestors of modern Trads and Conventions were championing literacy, agriculture, weaving, animal husbandry, and metalwork, for instance, and ministering to and protecting their respective cultures. What is distinctive about the period immediately prior to the founding of the Order - the time frame roughly analogous to the Dark Ages Mage era - is mages banding together into Fellowships and pursuing mystic attainment, artifacts, and personal magical power <i>instead </i>of attending to their fellow man. The Order of Hermes is obviously a chief offender here, but to a greater or lesser extent all of the mages of that time period are heavily focused on Mage Stuff, to the detriment of Sleeper society. It became very easy to consider the pursuit of enlightenment more important than helping the people around them.<br /> <br /> (I think we might credibly argue that the <i>mages </i>of the High Mythic Age are <i>more powerful </i>than their predecessors, with more nodes and artifacts in their grasp, but that <i>magic </i>is <i>less powerful </i>as a whole, as the mages have neglected to maintain its role in human life and has let bygone and spirit allies fall by the wayside in the pursuit of Wizard Politics)<br /> <br /> The Craftmasons - with their focus on humble, down-to-earth, stable magic and their commitment to &quot;the common man&quot; - are an outlier among the Fellowships of that era, and it's their influence that pushes the Order - and, later, the Traditions - to reconsider the mage relationship with Sleepers. I'm more critical of the Craftmasons than others (I think their stereotype in the fandom is more democratic than is merited from the text), but their contribution is very important - the other mages needed the kick in the ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T22:34:59-08:00","id":1290657,"title":"","content":"Somewhat misleading? How?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T01:27:22-08:00","id":1290687,"title":"","content":"As I said, they were by no means the first to provide magic to Sleepers - though it would be fair to say that the Craftmasons were exceptional in arguing for a return to those duties in the midst of an era where other mages (including their fellows in the OoR) were neglecting them. I also don't think it's particularly fruitful or accurate to use language like &quot;rallied to&quot; for the widespread adoption of the Order's paradigm - it was imposed <i>at least</i> as often as it was embraced. Nor would &quot;unity&quot; and &quot;cooperation&quot; be particularly apt to describe how the Order deals with outsiders or dissenters..<i>.</i><br /> <br /> (One could argue the Order's most significant advantage in the Ascension War lies in preparing for a fight more than a century before the other combatants knew there was going to be one.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T03:57:46-08:00","id":1290712,"title":"","content":"It's part of what they were about but it starts slipping at the end of the 1700s and by the mid 1800s and the Albertian Reforms there's been a (literal and metaphorical) hatchet job within the Order of Reason as it becomes the Technocratic Union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T04:03:38-08:00","id":1290715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290647-the-order-of-reason-for-the-man?p=1290712#post1290712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's part of what they were about but it starts slipping at the end of the 1700s and by the mid 1800s and the Albertian Reforms there's been a (literal and metaphorical) hatchet job within the Order of Reason as it becomes the Technocratic Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>Classic tragedy? Hero gets up, becomes powerful, takes over, and then gets corrupted by power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T05:29:39-08:00","id":1290722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290647-the-order-of-reason-for-the-man?p=1290715#post1290715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Classic tragedy? Hero gets up, becomes powerful, takes over, and then gets corrupted by power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much so. From &quot;We need to protect humanity from external threats&quot; to a paranoid &quot;We need to protect humanity from itself as well&quot; with a mixture of &quot;Big Brother knows what's best for you.&quot; tossed in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T19:42:24-08:00","id":1290971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290647-the-order-of-reason-for-the-man?p=1290722#post1290722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very much so. From &amp;quot;We need to protect humanity from external threats&amp;quot; to a paranoid &amp;quot;We need to protect humanity from itself as well&amp;quot; with a mixture of &amp;quot;Big Brother knows what's best for you.&amp;quot; tossed in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it'll be awesome if we had a game set of enterprising vampire hunters getting their hands on incendiary bombs and hand held flamethrowers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T02:40:28-08:00","id":1291052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290647-the-order-of-reason-for-the-man?p=1290712#post1290712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's part of what they were about but it starts slipping at the end of the 1700s and by the mid 1800s and the Albertian Reforms there's been a (literal and metaphorical) hatchet job within the Order of Reason as it becomes the Technocratic Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that once the Craftmasons - the Order's biggest proponents of the common man - were being killed and dissolved as a Convention, what would become the Technocratic Union was inevitably going to lose sight of their noble roots.<br /> <br /> That the High Guild transitioned seamlessly into the Syndicate, only gaining power in that time period, is probably further indicative of the Union's shifting priorities. Ditto also the secularizing of the Cabal of Pure Thought into the New World Order, and the loss of even the <i>pretense</i> of answering to a higher moral authority, that might have moderated their actions in favor of charity. (Which is not to say the Cabal of Pure Thought were ever particularly nice - they employed torture as an Instrument in their magick - just that they believed in something beyond the simple acquisition of power and control. The New World Order LIVES for nothing but Power and Control.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:27:02-08:00","id":1291062,"title":"","content":"Well, with Victorian Mage in development I imagine some further possible answers may be cropping up there too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:51:14-08:00","id":1291071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290647-the-order-of-reason-for-the-man?p=1291062#post1291062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, with Victorian Mage in development I imagine some further possible answers may be cropping up there too</div> </div> </div> </div>Victoria mage? Is it good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T03:52:59-08:00","id":1291074,"title":"","content":"I certainly hope so","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T05:36:23-08:00","id":1291100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290647-the-order-of-reason-for-the-man#post1290647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I'm rusty. Last time I read mage, it was a year ago. And it was progenitor, M20, toybox, and a few others.<br /> <br /> Question. Can I say that the order of reason, who transformed into the technocracy later on, was a champion of the common man? That they were the first ones to try and give magic into the common man. To try and give magic and power to the masses in the form of 'technology'. And so that's why people rallied to them, and their dedication and unity and cooperation, caused the people to rally to them. And that's how they won the war. By putting magic and power into the hands of the common man.<br /> <br /> Is what I said, correct, or at least, a reasonable interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a while since I've read that part, but as I recall it that's not <b>exactly</b> correct<br /> The Order of Reason was indeed championing for the common man, but they didn't want to give magic to the common man.<br /> Even with technology, they didn't want to &quot;putting magic and power in the hands of the common man.&quot;<br /> It was more like &quot;stripping the overpowered 1% of magic and power&quot; so that the common man wouldn't be a victim of those pesky mages anymore.<br /> It wasn't about redistribution of power and magic, it was more about &quot;no more magic for anyone&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, I'm sure in modern times there are softer ideals among the technocracy that want to &quot;put the power in the hands of the common man&quot;<br /> But I think it's that blur niche where the Traditions fit in.<br /> Otherwise the Technocracy would automatically be the good guys, no doubt. But things are a bit more... relative.<br /> <br /> The point is that a flexible reality is a problem because just a handful of people are Awakened, and so the Sleepers are helpless.<br /> While in a fixed reality (a completely static one) <b>no one</b> can alter reality, no one has power and so the playground is even for everyone.<br /> <br /> The counterargument of the Traditions is basically &quot;let's put the power in the hands of everyone for real&quot;, to Ascend humankind in an Awakened state.<br /> Reality returns to be flexible (as in ancient times) and people, the common man, can <b>truly</b> and <b>freely</b> decide what to do with it, and stop living in a fixed reality chosen by someone else (the Order of Reason)<br /> Which depending on personal trust towards humankind might be a good or bad idea. Optimism against pessimism, really.<br /> <br /> I don't remember in which book I've read a passage like this but I'm pretty sure there was one. I think it's the core premise. You have to choose if it's better for the common man to be master of its own fate on a metaphysical level, or master of its own fate in a metaphysically artificial playground.<br /> <br /> Funny thing yesterday I was explaining the setting to a friend and I said &quot;if you think about it, the Order of Reason were the good guys&quot;.<br /> But I'm not really sure about it. Which is interesting<br /> <br /> P.S. Victorian Mage sounds great","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T05:41:36-08:00","id":1291101,"title":"","content":"Grey settings are awesome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T09:53:23-08:00","id":1291163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290647-the-order-of-reason-for-the-man#post1290647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I'm rusty. Last time I read mage, it was a year ago. And it was progenitor, M20, toybox, and a few others.<br /> <br /> Question. Can I say that the order of reason, who transformed into the technocracy later on, was a champion of the common man? That they were the first ones to try and give magic into the common man. To try and give magic and power to the masses in the form of 'technology'. And so that's why people rallied to them, and their dedication and unity and cooperation, caused the people to rally to them. And that's how they won the war. By putting magic and power into the hands of the common man.<br /> <br /> Is what I said, correct, or at least, a reasonable interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could say that this was true to an extent about the Mages of the Order of Reason. However, I prefer the outlook on them that they were a faction of Mages who decided to follow outlooks and to act according to assumptions different from those of the Mystick Mages, and to develop different methods. The fact that this allowed them in some ways to better influence and direct the course of societies and groups of mundane humans was an additional, separate trait of the Order of Reason ; one that wasn't a principal trait of this group of Mages. I think that the Order of Reason were more concerned with gaining more influence and capabilities as a faction, and as individual Mages, than with helping the mundane humans to any considerable extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}